      {
        "id": 249002,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-11-06T11:05:15.980Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Alan Moore is a purist of the comic book medium, and has always been opposed to the idea of any sort of adaptation, solely because it is an adaptation.</p>\n<p>Also, it probably surprises no one that I actually wish the gunpowder treason had been successful.  I do find it odd that England celebrates an unsuccessful attempt at government overthrow.  Did the Crown encounter GFD to remind the people that rebellions fail, or did the government fail in suppressing the populace’s desire to celebrate what the Guy <em>tried</em> to accomplish?  Very strange to me.  I enjoy speculating on the possible alternate histories that might have resulted from different outcomes here.</p>\n<p>I am very intentionally not saying anything about any modern events which may or may not appear to parallel the actions of Mr. Fawkes.  As a reminder, discussion of politics does not belong on this server.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-11-06T11:05:15.980Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": 3,
