      {
        "id": 249003,
        "name": "",
        "username": "Thunderbird",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2022-11-06T14:52:35.714Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I <em>guess</em> I can see some of the author’s side, considering when you pour that much into a work you don’t want someone else messing with your child. Stephen King has definitely had opinions on his adaptations. King vs. Kubrick on <em>The Shining</em> is a battle of wills for the ages.</p>\n<p>Moore was just throwing around the <em>other</em> F-word (not opening the political can of worms here) in relation to comic books, when on its face <em>V</em> is totally opposed to that IMO.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-11-06T14:52:35.714Z",
